    "body": "## Problem\n\nFixes #42334\n\nWhen a terminal job or channel exits, `terminal_close()` clamps the exit-message overlay row to the last buffer line\n\nIf program output fills the terminal screen and does not end with a trailing newline, the cursor stays on the nonempty bottom row\n\nThe exit message overlay (`[Process exited 0]` or `[Terminal closed]`) then draws over and hides the final line of program output\n\n## Solution\n\nIn `src/nvim/terminal.c`, check whether a normal terminal close occurs with the cursor on the nonempty final line of the buffer\n\nWhen that occurs:\n- Send `\\r\\n` to the terminal via `terminal_receive()` to advance the row\n- Call `refresh_terminal()` again to display a blank row for the exit message\n\nExisting placement is preserved for:\n- Output that already ends with a newline\n- Short output that does not fill the screen\n- A bottom row that is already blank\n- Buffer deletion (`status == -1`)\n- Editor exit\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded regression tests:\n- `test/functional/terminal/channel_spec.lua`: adds 6 test cases covering 1, 6, and 100 output lines, each with and without trailing newline\n- `test/functional/terminal/ex_terminal_spec.lua`: adds a real PTY process test verifying screen and buffer content for output without trailing newline\n\nLocal verification on macOS arm64:\n- `make functionaltest TEST_FILE=test/functional/terminal`: 532 passed, 4 skipped\n- Related `termxx_spec.lua`, `autocmd_spec.lua`, and `defaults_spec.lua` suites: 62 passed\n- Debug build, Clint, Uncrustify, StyLua, clang-tidy 21 with macOS SDK, and EmmyLua checks passed\n- Pre-fix source fails 3 new regression cases and passes 4 controls, while fixed source passes all 7\n- Linux, Windows, and GitHub CI were not run locally\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-14T10:32:23Z",
